284 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 191 0 R
/T (Finding a classroom, laboratory, library, hostel, or auditorium can be difficult for new students and visitors on a large campus. A static map shows locations but does not automatically choose a connected walking route or respond to a closed walkway. AI Campus Navigation and Routers addresses this problem through a goal-based route-finding system.)
/E (Finding a classroom, laboratory, library, hostel, or auditorium can be difficult for new students and visitors on a large campus. A static map shows locations but does not automatically choose a connected walking route or respond to a closed walkway. AI Campus Navigation and Routers addresses this problem through a goal-based route-finding system.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
285 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 191 0 R
/T (The campus is represented as a weighted graph. Buildings and junctions form nodes, while walkways form edges with distance, closure status, and step-free information. The user selects a starting point and destination, or enters a supported place name. A destination resolver maps the input to a location identifier. The route planner filters unavailable edges and applies A* search to return a minimum-distance path for the selected constraints.)
/E (The campus is represented as a weighted graph. Buildings and junctions form nodes, while walkways form edges with distance, closure status, and step-free information. The user selects a starting point and destination, or enters a supported place name. A destination resolver maps the input to a location identifier. The route planner filters unavailable edges and applies A* search to return a minimum-distance path for the selected constraints.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
