<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 197 0 R
/T (A route finder can reduce the effort required to interpret a static campus map. It can also explain why a familiar shortcut is unavailable when a path is closed or contains stairs. These features are particularly useful for first-time users and for users who request step-free travel.)
/E (A route finder can reduce the effort required to interpret a static campus map. It can also explain why a familiar shortcut is unavailable when a path is closed or contains stairs. These features are particularly useful for first-time users and for users who request step-free travel.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
495 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 197 0 R
/T (The project focuses on a transparent search-based design. A user can inspect the selected path, distance, and constraint message rather than receiving an unexplained suggestion. This makes the system easier to demonstrate, test, and improve in an academic setting.)
/E (The project focuses on a transparent search-based design. A user can inspect the selected path, distance, and constraint message rather than receiving an unexplained suggestion. This makes the system easier to demonstrate, test, and improve in an academic setting.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [8]
>>
