/T (The graph is G = \(V, E\), where V is the set of locations and E is the set of walkways. An adjacency list stores the outgoing connections for each node. Each connection records its destination and weight. A bidirectional walkway creates one adjacency entry in each direction.)
/E (The graph is G = \(V, E\), where V is the set of locations and E is the set of walkways. An adjacency list stores the outgoing connections for each node. Each connection records its destination and weight. A bidirectional walkway creates one adjacency entry in each direction.)
