/T (A weighted graph matters because the fewest connections need not form the shortest walking route. A three-edge route may be shorter than a two-edge route if its individual walkways are short. Breadth-first search is suitable for minimizing hop count in an unweighted graph; it is not generally suitable for minimizing the varied distances used here [2].)
/E (A weighted graph matters because the fewest connections need not form the shortest walking route. A three-edge route may be shorter than a two-edge route if its individual walkways are short. Breadth-first search is suitable for minimizing hop count in an unweighted graph; it is not generally suitable for minimizing the varied distances used here [2].)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [7]
