/T (The reference implementation uses the Euclidean estimate h\(n\) = sqrt\(\(x\(n\)-x\(goal\)\)^2 + \(y\(n\)-y\(goal\)\)^2\). It measures straight-line distance in the same planar metre units as the sample edge weights. The estimate cannot include an arbitrary multiplier that would overstate the remaining distance.)
/E (The reference implementation uses the Euclidean estimate h\(n\) = sqrt\(\(x\(n\)-x\(goal\)\)^2 + \(y\(n\)-y\(goal\)\)^2\). It measures straight-line distance in the same planar metre units as the sample edge weights. The estimate cannot include an arbitrary multiplier that would overstate the remaining distance.)
