/T (For every sample edge \(u, v\), its weight is at least the straight-line distance between u and v. The triangle inequality then gives h\(u\) <= w\(u,v\) + h\(v\). This consistency property permits the graph-search implementation to finalize an expanded node without reopening it [3].)
/E (For every sample edge \(u, v\), its weight is at least the straight-line distance between u and v. The triangle inequality then gives h\(u\) <= w\(u,v\) + h\(v\). This consistency property permits the graph-search implementation to finalize an expanded node without reopening it [3].)
