/P 205 0 R
/T (A browser interface can render campus nodes, edges, selected routes, and user controls. The Canvas API supplies drawing primitives for such a map, while normal HTML controls can provide the location selection and textual result panel [4]. The renderer should take the planner's output as data rather than calculate an independent route. JavaScript classes and modules provide a way to separate the map model, search algorithm, lookup function, and presentation code [5], [6]. This separation allows a route to be tested directly with known inputs. It also makes it easier to update a map label without modifying the priority queue.)
/E (A browser interface can render campus nodes, edges, selected routes, and user controls. The Canvas API supplies drawing primitives for such a map, while normal HTML controls can provide the location selection and textual result panel [4]. The renderer should take the planner's output as data rather than calculate an independent route. JavaScript classes and modules provide a way to separate the map model, search algorithm, lookup function, and presentation code [5], [6]. This separation allows a route to be tested directly with known inputs. It also makes it easier to update a map label without modifying the priority queue.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [2]
