/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 212 0 R
/T (The evaluation distinguishes route-search correctness from interface usability and map accuracy. The first can be checked on a fixed graph with known weights. The second requires users and a working interface. The third requires a campus survey and an update process. The report verifies the first and defines how the other two can be assessed later.)
/E (The evaluation distinguishes route-search correctness from interface usability and map accuracy. The first can be checked on a fixed graph with known weights. The second requires users and a working interface. The third requires a campus survey and an update process. The report verifies the first and defines how the other two can be assessed later.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
797 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 212 0 R
/T (The reference program tests six named cases: a normal route, a step-free route, a closed shortcut, an isolated destination, a start equal to the destination, and a second ordinary destination. The expected distances are calculated from the graph. The test also checks alias resolution and an invalid node identifier.)
/E (The reference program tests six named cases: a normal route, a step-free route, a closed shortcut, an isolated destination, a start equal to the destination, and a second ordinary destination. The expected distances are calculated from the graph. The test also checks alias resolution and an invalid node identifier.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
