801 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 212 0 R
/T (A real map needs an owner, date, and method for recording closures. Changes should preserve stable identifiers and distinguish permanent geometry edits from temporary restrictions. A navigation result should identify the map snapshot on which it depends. Evaluation should also record errors explicitly. A no-route outcome can be correct when the destination is isolated. It should not be counted as an algorithm failure unless a permitted route actually exists. This distinction keeps the results interpretable.)
/E (A real map needs an owner, date, and method for recording closures. Changes should preserve stable identifiers and distinguish permanent geometry edits from temporary restrictions. A navigation result should identify the map snapshot on which it depends. Evaluation should also record errors explicitly. A no-route outcome can be correct when the destination is isolated. It should not be counted as an algorithm failure unless a permitted route actually exists. This distinction keeps the results interpretable.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [7]
>>
