1186 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 222 0 R
/T (A* does not guarantee that a user will arrive sooner in every real situation. The planner minimizes stored distance, while actual travel time can depend on crowds, waiting, weather, mobility, and access conditions. The estimated walking time is derived from a fixed assumed speed and is not a prediction trained on travel observations.)
/E (A* does not guarantee that a user will arrive sooner in every real situation. The planner minimizes stored distance, while actual travel time can depend on crowds, waiting, weather, mobility, and access conditions. The estimated walking time is derived from a fixed assumed speed and is not a prediction trained on travel observations.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1187 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 222 0 R
/T (The heuristic helps only when it provides useful information in compatible units. A small graph may not produce a noticeable interface speed difference even when the expansion count decreases. A larger evaluation should measure repeated runtime under a declared environment, rather than converting expansion counts directly into a speed claim.)
/E (The heuristic helps only when it provides useful information in compatible units. A small graph may not produce a noticeable interface speed difference even when the expansion count decreases. A larger evaluation should measure repeated runtime under a declared environment, rather than converting expansion counts directly into a speed claim.)
