2890 0 obj
<<
/Title (The campus is represented as a weighted graph. Buildings and junctions form nodes, while walkways form edges with distance, closure status, and step-free information. The user selects a starting point and destination, or enters a supported place name. A destination resolver maps the input to a location identifier. The route planner filters unavailable edges and applies A* search to return a minimum-distance path for the selected constraints.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2587 0 R
/Prev 2784 0 R
/Next 2906 0 R
>>
endobj
2891 0 obj
<<
/Title (The project demonstrates how search, state representation, constraints, and understandable route explanations can support campus travel. Future work includes a surveyed map, building-level indoor routes, location updates, multilingual input, and usability testing.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2587 0 R
/Prev 2907 0 R
/Next 2785 0 R
>>
