/Title (AI Campus Navigation and Routers applies classical AI search to a practical campus travel problem. It represents locations and walkways as a weighted graph, resolves a user's requested destination, filters route constraints, and computes an explainable minimum-distance path using A*.)
/Dest [46 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2788 0 R
/Next 2919 0 R
>>
endobj
2899 0 obj
<<
/Title (The main learning outcome is that useful navigation combines data, goals, constraints, and understandable output. The algorithm can only plan over the map it is given. Clear route explanations and a reliable map update process are therefore as important as the priority queue.)
/Dest [46 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2788 0 R
/Prev 2919 0 R
>>
endobj
