/Title (The reference implementation is written in JavaScript. A binary min-heap manages the search frontier, and a Euclidean heuristic guides the search. Dijkstra's algorithm is obtained by setting the heuristic to zero. The report includes illustrative map and interface diagrams, code extracts, route traces, and a defined evaluation method.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2587 0 R
/Prev 2890 0 R
/Next 2907 0 R
>>
endobj
2907 0 obj
<<
/Title (Tests on a ten-node teaching graph verify normal routes, step-free routing, walkway closure, an unreachable destination, and an already-reached destination. Both search modes match an independent all-pairs shortest-distance calculation across 400 start-destination cases covering four graph configurations. These checks validate the reference graph-search behavior; they do not measure field navigation or user travel performance.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2587 0 R
/Prev 2906 0 R
/Next 2891 0 R
>>
endobj
