2915 0 obj
<<
/Title (A* does not guarantee that a user will arrive sooner in every real situation. The planner minimizes stored distance, while actual travel time can depend on crowds, waiting, weather, mobility, and access conditions. The estimated walking time is derived from a fixed assumed speed and is not a prediction trained on travel observations.)
/Dest [45 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2787 0 R
/Prev 2896 0 R
/Next 2916 0 R
>>
endobj
2916 0 obj
<<
/Title (The heuristic helps only when it provides useful information in compatible units. A small graph may not produce a noticeable interface speed difference even when the expansion count decreases. A larger evaluation should measure repeated runtime under a declared environment, rather than converting expansion counts directly into a speed claim.)
/Dest [45 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2787 0 R
/Prev 2915 0 R
/Next 2897 0 R
>>
endobj
2917 0 obj
<<
/Title (A campus route finder can make directions more consistent by connecting destination names with permitted walkways and explicit preferences. A trace and distance explanation make its recommendations easier to inspect. Temporary closure filtering is especially useful when the available campus network changes.)
/Dest [45 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2897 0 R
/Next 2936 0 R
>>
endobj
2918 0 obj
<<
/Title (Indoor guidance and device positioning require additional engineering. GPS accuracy alone may not identify the correct doorway or floor. These capabilities should be added with their own validation rather than inferred from the success of the graph-search tests. The current report therefore provides a verified planning core, an implementation design, and a concrete next-step evaluation plan. It does not treat illustrative interface drawings as evidence of a field-tested navigation service.)
/Dest [45 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2897 0 R
/Prev 2936 0 R
>>
endobj
2919 0 obj
<<
/Title (The reference implementation demonstrates normal routing, step-free selection, closure-based replanning, unreachable destinations, and a zero-distance arrival case. Its A* and Dijkstra distances agree with an independent all-pairs calculation across 400 cases on four teaching graph configurations. Path reconstruction and edge-distance sums were also checked.)
/Dest [46 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2788 0 R
/Prev 2898 0 R
/Next 2899 0 R
>>
endobj
