/Title (An intelligent agent connects observations with actions in pursuit of a goal. The agents-and-environments framework is appropriate for navigation because the same movement has a different value depending on the destination and the available map [1]. For this project, the agent observes the chosen endpoints, graph snapshot, and route preference; it produces a route recommendation.)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3126 0 R
/Next 3149 0 R
>>
endobj
3149 0 obj
<<
/Title (A state-space formulation describes the current location and the legal transitions to neighboring locations. The search starts at one state and aims to reach a goal state. Once the map and constraints are fixed, a state can be represented by its node identifier. A predecessor record allows the final sequence of transitions to be reconstructed.)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3126 0 R
/Prev 3148 0 R
>>
endobj
3150 0 obj
<<
/Title (The graph is G = \(V, E\), where V is the set of locations and E is the set of walkways. An adjacency list stores the outgoing connections for each node. Each connection records its destination and weight. A bidirectional walkway creates one adjacency entry in each direction.)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3127 0 R
/Next 3166 0 R
>>
endobj
3151 0 obj
<<
/Title (The cost of a route is the sum of its edge weights. The current project minimizes example walking distance. If the objective changes to travel time or perceived effort, both the edge costs and the heuristic must be reconsidered. A route described as "best" should always identify the criterion being minimized.)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3127 0 R
/Prev 3166 0 R
>>
endobj
3152 0 obj
<<
/Title (Dijkstra search selects the frontier entry with the smallest accumulated path cost. On a finite graph with nonnegative weights, it returns a minimum-cost route when the goal is selected for expansion. It does not use a goal-directed estimate [2]. In the reference implementation, this mode is produced by setting the heuristic to zero.)
/Dest [27 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3128 0 R
/Next 3167 0 R
>>
endobj
